{
  "_id": "tg-hardheartedness",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "I will harden his heart, that he shall not let the people go, Ex. 4:21 (7:3; 10:1; 14:4, 17). hardened his spirit, and made his heart obstinate, Deut. 2:30. thou shalt not harden thine heart, Deut. 15:7. Let me not hear again the voice of the Lord, Deut. 18:16. do ye harden your hearts, as the Egyptians and Pharaoh hardened their hearts, 1 Sam. 6:6. hardened their necks, like … their fathers, 2 Kgs. 17:14. he stiffened his neck, and hardened his heart, 2 Chr. 36:13. who hath hardened himself against him, and hath prospered, Job 9:4. Harden not your heart, as in the provocation, Ps. 95:8 (Heb. 3:8, 15; 4:7). wicked man hardeneth his face, Prov. 21:29. he that hardeneth his heart shall fall into mischief, Prov. 28:14. have removed their heart far from me, Isa. 29:13. ye stouthearted, that are far from righteousness, Isa. 46:12. hardened our heart from thy fear, Isa. 63:17. they hearkened not unto me … but hardened their neck, Jer. 7:26. all the house of Israel are impudent and hardhearted, Ezek. 3:7. his mind hardened in pride, Dan. 5:20.",
