    {
      "text": "hardness of their hearts and the blindness of their minds, 1 Ne. 14:7 (Alma 13:4). nothing … could soften their hearts, 1 Ne. 18:20. against him will they harden their hearts, 1 Ne. 22:5. after they have hardened their hearts, 2 Ne. 6:10. they hardened their hearts … have been destroyed, 2 Ne. 25:10. harden their hearts against the Holy Spirit, 2 Ne. 33:2. they hardened their hearts, and understood not, Mosiah 3:15. eyes … blinded; therefore they hardened their hearts, Mosiah 11:29. he that will harden his heart, the same receiveth the lesser portion, Alma 12:10. let us repent, and harden not our hearts, Alma 12:37 (34:31). they become more hardened, and thus their state becomes worse, Alma 24:30. Spirit … began to withdraw … because of the wickedness and the hardness of their hearts, Hel. 6:35. Because of the hardness of the hearts … I will take away my word, Hel. 13:8. if they shall harden their hearts against me I will return their iniquities, 3 Ne. 20:28. repent … and harden not their hearts, 3 Ne. 21:22. power of Satan who did get hold upon their hearts, 4 Ne. 1:28 (Ether 15:19). prayer … without faith, because of the hardness of their hearts, Morm. 3:12. devil … hath hardened the hearts of men, Ether 8:25. when I use no sharpness they harden their hearts, Moro. 9:4.",
